2026-10-09T18:49:03.0201429Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0211770Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0314939Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0325440Z [0m
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0326307Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0326862Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0327101Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0327878Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0328690Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0329005Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0329277Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0330201Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0330392Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0330893Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0331748Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0332572Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0333197Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0333487Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0333902Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0334378Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0334924Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0335536Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0335682Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0335820Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0335985Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0336391Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0336899Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0338932Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0339108Z I will:
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0339337Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0339912Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0340577Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0341386Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0341913Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0342190Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0342483Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0342917Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0343287Z    /root
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0354990Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0355926Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0368806Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0370168Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0370640Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0373765Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0374783Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0390110Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0390893Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0401517Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0402228Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0403025Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0403365Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0403667Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0404071Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0404525Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0405501Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0406006Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0406291Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0406610Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0406794Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0407014Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0407365Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0407504Z 
2026-10-09T18:49:03.0407518Z 
